Hi,

I've noticed a few things with the newest Spork release on
sporkhack.com, and was wondering if anyone could replicate these and
shed a bit of light on possible bugs:

1) Eating floating eye corpses gives no messages after the first eye.
This may be because more floating eyes don't give greater radius of
telepathy, and thus not a bug - but that's not what it looks like to
me.

2) The 'remember last thing I wrote' feature has a strange bug that
appears to come and go: there seems to be some problem with the "--
more--" messages when they appear in the middle of these strings.  On
my terminal (putty on WinXp), it sometimes causes a wrap around to the
next line that can't be deleted with backspace.  I'll try and get a
less vague rep on this if I can replicate what's going on and explain
it in more detail - maybe someone else has more details?

3) I can't use #name - (n) on weapons.  Is this new to this release?
It may be a side effect of the 'Staff of X' addition, or maybe it's
even older, and just not been picked up because nobody bothers trying
to name weapons.  I tried on a staff because I was offered 2zm for it
(and wanted to distinguish it from other staves later).  I can use
#name - (y) on everything fine.  The only other class of items that
fails on #name - (n) seems to be comestibles.

